Package: speakerguardd
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Feed-forward speaker protection for the MacBook Neo (J700)
 speakerguardd 0.1 protects the speakers of Apple Silicon Macs whose
 amplifiers have no voltage and current sense, the MacBook Neo (J700), with a
 thermal model driven by the audio it is fed. Until the daemon holds the
 sound card's volume lock, the kernel keeps the speakers at their safe level.
 .
 udev starts it for the J700 speaker card; on the J700 speakersafetyd does not
 start. Where speakerguardd v2 is installed, its gate decides at every boot
 whether this daemon or v2 holds the speakers.
 .
 speakerguardd 0.1 is deprecated and will be removed; aurora-speaker-upgrade
 moves a Mac to speakerguardd v2.
